1
00:00:03,342 --> 00:00:07,331
But Earth is just one point in a much bigger family.

2
00:00:07,631 --> 00:00:10,074
At the center of everything is the Sun.

3
00:00:10,973 --> 00:00:15,095
The star that gives light and warmth to us all.

4
00:00:15,395 --> 00:00:18,584
Mercury — the planet closest to the Sun.

5
00:00:18,884 --> 00:00:23,646
Venus is the hottest planet, beneath dense sulfuric-acid clouds.

6
00:00:23,946 --> 00:00:28,175
Earth is the only place where we have found life in our solar system.

7
00:00:28,475 --> 00:00:32,196
Mars — the red world humans dream of visiting.

8
00:00:32,496 --> 00:00:35,472
Jupiter — the giant of the solar system.

9
00:00:35,838 --> 00:00:38,654
A churning storm larger than the entire Earth.

10
00:00:42,521 --> 00:00:45,390
Rings made of ice and rock — millions of pieces.

11
00:00:45,863 --> 00:00:49,319
Uranus — an ice giant rolling on its side.

12
00:00:49,619 --> 00:00:53,661
Neptune — the farthest, coldest world, with winds beyond any storm.

13
00:00:53,961 --> 00:00:57,471
Farther out lies the Kuiper Belt, home to icy bodies.

14
00:00:57,771 --> 00:01:01,280
All of it turning around the Sun in perfect rhythm.

15
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:05,729
From so very far away, Earth becomes a faint pale blue dot.

16
00:01:06,029 --> 00:01:09,165
Our only home — in a vast, wide universe.

